It is possible to code like this:

```
(system_a, system_b).before(system_c)
```

But it is not possible (using public API) to add structure to this code:

```
fn some_systems() -> SystemConfigs {
  // Because `into_configs()` is not public
  (system_a, system_b).into_configs()
}

// Because type parameter is complicated
fn some_systems() -> IntoSystemConfigs<???> {
  (system_a, system_b)
}

some_systems().before(system_c)
```

Moreover, it is possible to create `SystemConfigs` using some dummy label:

```
fn some_systems() -> SystemConfigs {
  (system_a, system_b).before(dummy_system)
}
```

so hiding `into_configs` does not do much.

Bevy 0.12.0.
